From fcec8d1326a4d4752b5974d05408ba6d16bd19c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 15:49:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 241/913] drivers: regulator: use DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM()

Replace DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER() directives with DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM()
for resources that need to be unpaged for PM sequence support. This
change covers the resources used by generic core and stm32mp15
platforms.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 24f5c5eeeb5598b0bfd23d793f96187681d88f1a drivers: regulator: use DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM()]
Change-Id: I81859e26190e9f0a1223b1c1ba83bf81560e5281
Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/regulator/stm32_vrefbuf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/regulator/stm32_vrefbuf.c b/core/drivers/regulator/stm32_vrefbuf.c
index 23675feac..574e29f85 100644
--- a/core/drivers/regulator/stm32_vrefbuf.c
+++ b/core/drivers/regulator/stm32_vrefbuf.c
@@ -307,7 +307,7 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_vrefbuf_pm(enum pm_op op, unsigned int pm_hint __unused,
 
 	return TEE_SUCCESS;
 }
-DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER(stm32_vrefbuf_pm);
+DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM(stm32_vrefbuf_pm);
 
 static TEE_Result stm32_vrefbuf_init(struct regulator *regulator,
 				     const void *fdt __unused,
-- 
2.53.0

